, O Rāvana, conclude peace with Rāma-king of men. Having ascertained fit course, do you act properly.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.433,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-35-31","DUTT-6-35-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6026030","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d9095cd771ff61d7e1fe74db5a87ca759d14814569d525881df7c904c58b7d14","compact":"9e9e7a3a7a4c0146983c9c7a6d2b9b67dd71b17f3fdfaeeee7c929e92b9bba1b","nasal":"46f022ce60fc577821759be70d1eee1d83e94a3fec004e06a8259f12cc676b79"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-26-31","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":26,"verse":31,"english":"These and other evil omens occur. Rama I deem as Vişnnu assuming the form of a man. Rāghava of steady prowess, for certain, is no human being, he that has built a bridge over the deep, must be an exceedingly wonderful person. Therefore, O Rāvana, conclude peace with Rāma-king of men. Having ascertained fit course, do you act properly.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.836,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-35-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6026031","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fdc9d3ad25d0b70d674a0f8c89e47d343d611d2d167077c12738d22c07080058","compact":"bbeaf6048de68a87294cf54901bc4173670008f788677b2274a54902df6f5d5d","nasal":"bbeaf6048de68a87294cf54901bc4173670008f788677b2274a54902df6f5d5d"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-26-32","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":26,"verse":32,"english":"These and other evil omens occur. Rama I deem as Vişnnu assuming the form of a man. Rāghava of steady prowess, for certain, is no human being, he that has built a bridge over the deep, must be an exceedingly wonderful person. Therefore, O Rāvana, conclude peace with Rāma-king of men. Having ascertained fit course, do you act properly.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.352,"method":"s